## Major Architecture Change: Independent Crons Replace Heartbeat Dispatcher
### Problem Diagnosed
- Heartbeat was dispatching 107 times/day but only 1 article published
- Root cause: heartbeat (depth 0) → spawns subagent (depth 1) → subagent needs 6 critics (depth 2 = max)
- Subagents were completing research/draft files but failing to update status.json
- Pipeline stalled because scheduler saw "DRAFT in progress" and dispatched nothing new
- 11 research files sitting in LITF drafts, never advancing

### New Architecture
- Heartbeat: 30m interval (was 10m), P0 checks ONLY — no article dispatching
- `article-litf`: 2h interval, autonomous worker, does ALL phases in one run
- `article-crashreport`: 2h interval, offset 30m, autonomous
- `article-aihome`: 2h interval, offset 1h, autonomous
- `technically-legal-iterate`: 1h interval (unchanged)
- Each worker reads its own status.json, does research→draft→critique→ship→qa
- No subagent spawning — the cron IS the worker
- #1 rule: ALWAYS update status.json before exiting

### Moltbook Cron Updated
- Was spawning subagent (same depth problem) — now does all work itself
- Full pipeline: fetch feed → pick story → research → draft → critique → ship → QA

